{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GunG7qhVkjEcsLRNa87cAY","type":"tool_result","content":"x describe: ok: material: 18 fields, 29 entries\nMaterials as data with three.js's classic parameters (color, map, roughness, emissive, flags); the engine decides how to draw them.\nfallback: material:default\nids: material:asphalt, material:barrel, material:barrelLid, material:barrelStaves, material:blobShadow, material:brick, material:carpet, material:checker, material:cloth, material:concrete, material:crate, material:default, material:flagstone, material:flame, material:glass, material:glow, material:hallFloor, material:iron, material:paint, … (10 more; all 29 in out/describe/material/describe.json)\n  description: string, = \"\": What it is for, in plain sentences.\n  color: string, = \"#ffffff\": The base colour, hex; it multiplies the map (three.js's color).\nx describe: ok: texture: 7 fields, 24 entries\nSeeded, periodic texture generators: colour, height, roughness and emissive per texel, with their parameters, size, tile, density and look.\nids: texture:asphalt, texture:brick, texture:carpet, texture:checker, texture:concrete, texture:crate, texture:dirt, texture:flagstone, texture:glass, texture:grass, texture:hallFloor, texture:metal, texture:moss, texture:planks, texture:plaster, texture:runes, texture:shingles, texture:siding, texture:staves, texture:stone, texture:tiles, texture:wallpaper, texture:water, texture:wood\n  description: string, required: What it draws, in plain sentences.\n  params: object, = {}: Its parameters as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts: type, default, description, minimum…), each with a defaul...\nx describe: ok: geometry: 4 fields, 7 entries\nShapes props, levels and bodies name by id: a builder of a three.js BufferGeometry with its parameters and a vertex budget.\nfallback: geometry:box\nids: geometry:box, geometry:frustum, geometry:limb, geometry:pillar, geometry:ramp, geometry:ring, geometry