{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014u9AypBp3rEa8oHiRHnJdZ","type":"tool_result","content":"// T0 project: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: the labs, the fixtures, the tools, the test pages,\n// specs and helpers, the Claude Code hooks and the root configs (tsconfig.check.json).\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"composite\": true,\n    \"emitDeclarationOnly\": true,\n    \"rootDir\": \".\",\n    \"outDir\": \"node_modules/.cache/tsc\"\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"labs\", \"fixtures\", \"tools\", \"tests\", \".claude/hooks\", \"*.config.ts\", \"package-lock.json\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"**/*.test.ts\"],\n  \"references\": [{ \"path\": \"./tsconfig.engine.json\" }]\n}\n// T0's type check (`npm run typecheck`, inside `npm run check`): `tsc -b` over three composite projects that emit\n// declarations only, into node_modules/.cache/tsc/. A run skips a project whose own files and upstream declarations\n// did not change, and re-checks only what a change can reach (ADR-0014, amendment 7). Together the projects hold\n// exactly tsconfig.json's files, each once (tools/checkAll.test.ts checks it):\n// - tsconfig.engine.json: engine/, without its tests. The engine imports nothing outside it (PLAN.md §6.1).\n// - tsconfig.apps.json: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: labs/, fixtures/, tools/, tests/ (pages,\n//   specs, setup, helpers), .claude/hooks/ and the root *.config.ts.\n// - tsconfig.tests.json: every *.test.ts, which may import anything.\n// A new directory under those roots joins its project by itself; a new root directory joins tsconfig.json's\n// \"include\" and one project's. A project reaches another's files only through \"references\" (tsc's TS6307 names a\n// file outside them): add the reference, never the file to a second project. Each project lists package-lock.json,\n// because tsc -b skips a project by its own files alone: a dependency change must rebuild it.\n{\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"references\": [\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.engine.json\" },\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.apps.json\" },\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.tests.json\" }\n  ]\n}\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:2: * @file The animation library's files (`data/anim/sets/<set>/*.json`) as text, in one chunk: the pages that register\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:16: * const [path, read] = Object.entries(CLIP_FILES)[0]; // ['../../data/anim/sets/<set>/<file>.json', …]\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:22:/** Every clip set's files, by path (`../../data/anim/sets/<set>/<file>.json`), as their text. */","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e83c655a-6d0a-42b2-ac8e-79c6fd4e6b22","uuid":"1ce4cb89-49b3-461d-93d2-6e7e12aeae75","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:30:00.252Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// T0 project: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: the labs, the fixtures, the tools, the test pages,\n// specs and helpers, the Claude Code hooks and the root configs (tsconfig.check.json).\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"composite\": true,\n    \"emitDeclarationOnly\": true,\n    \"rootDir\": \".\",\n    \"outDir\": \"node_modules/.cache/tsc\"\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"labs\", \"fixtures\", \"tools\", \"tests\", \".claude/hooks\", \"*.config.ts\", \"package-lock.json\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"**/*.test.ts\"],\n  \"references\": [{ \"path\": \"./tsconfig.engine.json\" }]\n}\n// T0's type check (`npm run typecheck`, inside `npm run check`): `tsc -b` over three composite projects that emit\n// declarations only, into node_modules/.cache/tsc/. A run skips a project whose own files and upstream declarations\n// did not change, and re-checks only what a change can reach (ADR-0014, amendment 7). Together the projects hold\n// exactly tsconfig.json's files, each once (tools/checkAll.test.ts checks it):\n// - tsconfig.engine.json: engine/, without its tests. The engine imports nothing outside it (PLAN.md §6.1).\n// - tsconfig.apps.json: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: labs/, fixtures/, tools/, tests/ (pages,\n//   specs, setup, helpers), .claude/hooks/ and the root *.config.ts.\n// - tsconfig.tests.json: every *.test.ts, which may import anything.\n// A new directory under those roots joins its project by itself; a new root directory joins tsconfig.json's\n// \"include\" and one project's. A project reaches another's files only through \"references\" (tsc's TS6307 names a\n// file outside them): add the reference, never the file to a second project. Each project lists package-lock.json,\n// because tsc -b skips a project by its own files alone: a dependency change must rebuild it.\n{\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"references\": [\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.engine.json\" },\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.apps.json\" },\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.tests.json\" }\n  ]\n}\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:2: * @file The animation library's files (`data/anim/sets/<set>/*.json`) as text, in one chunk: the pages that register\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:16: * const [path, read] = Object.entries(CLIP_FILES)[0]; // ['../../data/anim/sets/<set>/<file>.json', …]\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:22:/** Every clip set's files, by path (`../../data/anim/sets/<set>/<file>.json`), as their text. */","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014u9AypBp3rEa8oHiRHnJdZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
