{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MwzeQXbqysa7fkF2njFnTg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Engine feedback: wobble\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 6a1501f) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\n\n## Friction\n\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\n# The starter game\n\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\n\n## The game\n\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\n\n## Files\n\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e83c655a-6d0a-42b2-ac8e-79c6fd4e6b22","uuid":"70f60e6f-7fb1-4378-8485-c8c3f618e58a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T12:40:54.524Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Engine feedback: wobble\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 6a1501f) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\n\n## Friction\n\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\n# The starter game\n\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\n\n## The game\n\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\n\n## Files\n\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MwzeQXbqysa7fkF2njFnTg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjoDaNe6FCnzqK9Lp1fg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JhdmHaNNKLmGUyU9wbmzc1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine feedback: Well Wobbled\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 6a1501f) and did not get. Written for an engine agent who has never seen\nthis repository.\n\n## Requests\n\n1. **A page that can change scene.** A running page cannot switch scenes, so the hub's session scene (`game:round`) had to be a second,\n   separate scene picked at load by `?scene=`, with its own setup that repeats the pavilion. A `engine.setScene(id)` would let one\n   scene library serve the title, the island and a session.\n2. **`getTerrain` should cache.** Calling `getTerrain('terrain:x')` builds a new 240 × 240 heightfield each time. My first draft called it from\n   `groundAt(x, z)` inside systems and a step cost 650 ms, and island setup took 106 s, until I cached the result in the game. Either cache\n   inside `getTerrain` by id, or say in its comment that it is a builder, not a lookup.\n3. **A way to read a custom, edge-triggered button.** `input.pressed(action)` is \"pressed at the last sample\", and a frame that runs several steps\n   misses presses. In the page, `onFrame` can only see the last sample. I latched presses in the sim instead (a counter on a component, from a\n   `values` custom intent). A `input.pressedSince(frame)` or an event queue would be simpler.\n4. **Tinting an actor.** There is no per-actor colour, so every seat colour (the hub's four) and every tracksuit colour is a separate `defineBody`.\n   A `tint` on `spawnActor`/`crowdBody` would remove a dozen near-copies.\n5. **Playing a pose clip at a time without a one-shot slot.** Scrubbing slot `t` by hand works (and is data), but `playClip` with `speed: 0` plus\n   `seekClip` only reaches the top clip. A `scrubClip(w, id, clip, t)` would make \"the thumb is the exercise\" a one-line idea.\n\n## Friction\n\n- `createEngine` calls `input.use(mapFor())` on every sample, with `mapFor()` from the `actionMap` option (default `actionMap:thirdPerson`). My calls to\n  `engine.input.use('actionMap:roam')` were silently overridden each frame, so no custom action worked until I passed `actionMap: () => myMap`.\n  The `input.use` comment does not say so; the `actionMap` option should be the only documented way, or `use` should stick.\n- JSON imports: the plan and the guide say a static `import rest from './rest.json' with { type: 'json' }` passes lint and Node, but `tsc -b`\n  (TS6307) says the file is not in the project, because the labs include globs are `.ts` only. I converted the JSON to a `.ts` module.\n- Entities spawned in `setup` (or in a step) join at the end of the step, so `w.add(id, 'seat', …)` right after `spawnActor` throws\n  `SIM_NO_ENTITY`. `spawnActor`'s `components` option is the fix, but nothing points to it from the error.\n- A component array that grows past its declared length leaves holes (`undefined`), which is `SIM_NOT_DATA` at the next capture, far from the write. The\n  message names no component or index.\n- `ScenePropComponents` / `query('sceneProp')` is not a key of the game's own component type, so reading props sim-side needs a cast.\n- `npm run check` fails a game on an 400+ line file as a warning and 600 as an error, which is fine, but prettier then expands dense lines and can\n  triple a file's length. Splitting after formatting is more work than splitting before; say so in AGENTS.md.\n- `node x new <kind>` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` for a game (as the plan warned); I wrote the entries by hand instead.\n- Software-rendered WebGPU in Chromium takes 3 s a frame around the pavilion (754 draw calls, 835k triangles), and a screenshot taken before the first\n  frame of a new area is solid black. That is not an engine fault, but a `__engine.whenFrame()` to await would save guessing waits.\n\n## Local engine patches\n\nNone. `npm run check` reports the engine as pinned.\nEOF\ncat out/hub2.log | cut -c1-300 | tail -4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":956,"cache_read_input_tokens":578909,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":956},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e83c655a-6d0a-42b2-ac8e-79c6fd4e6b22","uuid":"3cc52863-e1f8-4c89-8ddc-9f335d747051","timestamp":"2026-11-05T12:41:08.538Z","request_id":"req_011CgjoDa7WSGUXschsJbWrg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JhdmHaNNKLmGUyU9wbmzc1":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-031600__x54facc/work/WellWobbled-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-031600 && cat > ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine feedback: Well Wobbled\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 6a1501f) and did not get. Written for an engine agent who has never seen\nthis repository.\n\n## Requests\n\n1. **A page that can change scene.** A running page cannot switch scenes, so the hub's session scene (`game:round`) had to be a second,\n   separate scene picked at load by `?scene=`, with its own setup that repeats the pavilion. A `engine.setScene(id)` would let one\n   scene library serve the title, the island and a session.\n2. **`getTerrain` should cache.** Calling `getTerrain('terrain:x')` builds a new 240 × 240 heightfield each time. My first draft called it from\n   `groundAt(x, z)` inside systems and a step cost 650 ms, and island setup took 106 s, until I cached the result in the game. Either cache\n   inside `getTerrain` by id, or say in its comment that it is a builder, not a lookup.\n3. **A way to read a custom, edge-triggered button.** `input.pressed(action)` is \"pressed at the last sample\", and a frame that runs several steps\n   misses presses. In the page, `onFrame` can only see the last sample. I latched presses in the sim instead (a counter on a component, from a\n   `values` custom intent). A `input.pressedSince(frame)` or an event queue would be simpler.\n4. **Tinting an actor.** There is no per-actor colour, so every seat colour (the hub's four) and every tracksuit colour is a separate `defineBody`.\n   A `tint` on `spawnActor`/`crowdBody` would remove a dozen near-copies.\n5. **Playing a pose clip at a time without a one-shot slot.** Scrubbing slot `t` by hand works (and is data), but `playClip` with `speed: 0` plus\n   `seekClip` only reaches the top clip. A `scrubClip(w, id, clip, t)` would make \"the thumb is the exercise\" a one-line idea.\n\n## Friction\n\n- `createEngine` calls `input.use(mapFor())` on every sample, with `mapFor()` from the `actionMap` option (default `actionMap:thirdPerson`). My calls to\n  `engine.input.use('actionMap:roam')` were silently overridden each frame, so no custom action worked until I passed `actionMap: () => myMap`.\n  The `input.use` comment does not say so; the `actionMap` option should be the only documented way, or `use` should stick.\n- JSON imports: the plan and the guide say a static `import rest from './rest.json' with { type: 'json' }` passes lint and Node, but `tsc -b`\n  (TS6307) says the file is not in the project, because the labs include globs are `.ts` only. I converted the JSON to a `.ts` module.\n- Entities spawned in `setup` (or in a step) join at the end of the step, so `w.add(id, 'seat', …)` right after `spawnActor` throws\n  `SIM_NO_ENTITY`. `spawnActor`'s `components` option is the fix, but nothing points to it from the error.\n- A component array that grows past its declared length leaves holes (`undefined`), which is `SIM_NOT_DATA` at the next capture, far from the write. The\n  message names no component or index.\n- `ScenePropComponents` / `query('sceneProp')` is not a key of the game's own component type, so reading props sim-side needs a cast.\n- `npm run check` fails a game on an 400+ line file as a warning and 600 as an error, which is fine, but prettier then expands dense lines and can\n  triple a file's length. Splitting after formatting is more work than splitting before; say so in AGENTS.md.\n- `node x new <kind>` prints `NEW_DOCS` lines about `labs/playground/…` for a game (as the plan warned); I wrote the entries by hand instead.\n- Software-rendered WebGPU in Chromium takes 3 s a frame around the pavilion (754 draw calls, 835k triangles), and a screenshot taken before the first\n  frame of a new area is solid black. That is not an engine fault, but a `__engine.whenFrame()` to await would save guessing waits.\n\n## Local engine patches\n\nNone. `npm run check` reports the engine as pinned.\nEOF\ncat out/hub2.log | cut -c1-300 | tail -4"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01JhdmHaNNKLmGUyU9wbmzc1":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-031600__x54facc/work/WellWobbled-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-031600"}}}
