{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk1HbFER7dt8aC9BG6wC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added Plumb's plait and the Gull and Frog, but the stop condition is still not met. The browser stage on the final build still crashes, so I've stopped.\n\n**Added this round**\n- Plumb is now spawned with a ponytail, so the plait has secondary motion.\n- The Gull and Frog are in the world as small actors, on the plaza and at the pond. They don't yet have talk prompts or any behaviour.\n- The rebuilt island still runs headless in Node, and `npm run check` passes. The single HTML is rebuilt, boots in Chromium with no engine errors, and shows the title screen with music at 0.1.\n\n**Still not done**\n- **Browser stage:** the full run crashes with \"Target crashed\", this time at the first key press after Begin, when the island scene starts rendering. I assume memory pressure or the GPU on this shared machine, but I didn't confirm which. Earlier I got 18 of 20 browser checks on an older build.\n- **Screens not viewed:** I haven't checked the Programme, pond, line, results, pause, Dev Mode and About screens by eye or by script.\n- **Not built:** the headband and the 20/30-pebble tracksuit colours.\n- **Test run not shown whole:** the last whole-suite run lost a worker, so I never saw all 25 files pass in one run. I re-ran the heavy files separately (playthrough, rules, round, attract, island) and they pass. I did not re-run the individual balance files after the Gull/Frog change.\n\nNo further browser pass is possible while the machine can't keep a page alive through the island scene."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":513,"cache_read_input_tokens":668345,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":513},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","spe