{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkBFKnAUXPFgWus5u9o4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both the full suite and the browser stage now pass on the final build, so everything I could verify here is verified.\n\n- **Tests:** all 25 `labs/game` files (40 tests) pass in one run on the final code, which includes the Gull and Frog wandering. `npm run check` passes.\n- **Browser stage:** 42 of 42 checks pass on the final build.\n- **Hub harness:** passes at 2, 3 and 4 players and with the host leaving, on this build. The host-leave run passed after the Gull and Frog change; the 2, 3 and 4 player runs were on the build just before it.\n- **Browser test fix:** one run failed 9 checks because attract started while the slow page was still booting, before the test pressed anything. That was a timing flaw in my test, not in the game. The test now leaves attract first, as a player would, and allows a wider window for attract to start.\n\nI never opened the Line screenshot, and I never saw the Gull and Frog moving or Plumb's plait swing in a browser. The first two run in the sim and the Line HUD reads correctly. The plait is only known to spawn without error. Everything TASK.md asks for is in `work/`: the single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":892,"cache_read_input_tokens":703039,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":892},"output_tokens":401,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e83c655a-6d0a-42b2-ac8e-79c6fd4e6b22","uuid":"ec1e25ee-58b6-475e-94a8-96e3514d8372","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:29:52.092Z","request_id":"req_011CgkBFJggXJZZW7BurSyrH"}
