{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkK8FrmKoGTLRveKq3ba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything I can check on this machine now passes on the final build, apart from the Gull, Frog and plait not being seen in a browser.\n\n- **The Line:** the guest now really walks it. I added an invisible walkway under the rope and the guest is placed along it. In a headless run the perfect bot reaches 21.75 m of 40 after 12 s while the guest's position moves along the rope (z 68.8 to 86.8). Line balance still passes (perfect 1000, human 1000, sloppy 806, idle 0 on the earlier 3-seed runs).\n- **Gull, Frog and Plumb's plait:** a new test, `critters.test.ts`, passes in the headless sim. It checks that the Gull wanders more than 1 m and the Frog hops, that Plumb carries the plait's secondary-motion component, and that the guest walks the line. I have **not** seen any of these in a browser: the three browser attempts I made (two loads and the critters script) crashed with \"Target crashed\" at 3–4 GB of free memory, so that evidence is sim-only.\n- **Whole suite:** all 26 `labs/game` files (41 tests) pass in one run on the final code.\n- **Browser stage:** 42 of 42 checks pass on this build. An earlier run on this build failed 8 checks because attract started during a slow boot; I fixed the test to leave attract with a pad press, as a player would, and the rerun passed.\n- **`npm run check`:** passes.\n- **Hub harness:** not re-run after the walkway change. It passed 2, 3, 4 players and with the host leaving on the build just before it.\n\nThe single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are all in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":728827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260},"output_tokens":558,"service_tier":"stand