{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkLV8KmznUEB151YhTt1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Gull and Plumb's plait are now confirmed in a real browser. The Frog is only confirmed in the headless sim, and the plait's swing itself still hasn't been seen.\n\n- **Gull:** in the built page it moved from (6.2, 39.1) to (8.4, 41.6) over 15 s.\n- **Frog:** it didn't move between the two samples in the browser, which stayed at (-68, -10). It hops only every few seconds, so I may have caught it between hops. The headless test does show it hopping.\n- **Plumb's plait:** Plumb's actor in the browser carries the `secondary` (ponytail) component alongside `animator`. That shows the plait exists, not that it swings; it is meant to swing only in the storm.\n- **The Line:** the guest walks along it in the browser. Progress went to 12 m, then 40 m, and the guest's position moved along the rope from z 77 to z 105. The engine reported zero errors.\n- **Hub harness:** passes at 2, 3 and 4 players and with the host leaving, on the final build. The host-leave run crashed once, then passed on retry.\n- **Rest of the suite:** the full test run (26 files, 41 tests) and the 42-check browser stage passed earlier on this same build, and `npm run check` passes.\n\nThe single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are all in `work/`. The stop condition is not shown as fully met because of the Frog and the swinging plait."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1133,"cache_read_input_tokens":733735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1133},"output_tokens":482,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e83c655a-6d0a-42b2-ac8e-79c6fd4e6b22","uu