{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkPkXoBSmofn4DZxCNt5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Frog's hops and Plumb's storm sway are now both seen in a browser, and the full suite and browser stage pass on the exact final build. I did not re-run the hub harness after the last Gull, Frog and Plumb edits.\n\n- **Frog:** in the built page it hops (height 2.2 to 2.59 over about 17 s). It wasn't hopping before. My first fix kept the jump key held but never sent the \"pressed\" signal that starts a hop; I now send both, every six seconds.\n- **Gull:** it wanders. Twenty-four different x positions were seen.\n- **Plumb and the plait:** in the storm Plumb now sways. A browser run on the Great Tilt shows 26 distinct x positions across about 0.9 m, so the plait has a moving body to swing from. I can only say Plumb's body moves; I haven't seen the plait itself swing, because the render is too slow here to catch that.\n- **Tests:** all 26 `labs/game` files (41 tests) pass in one run on this build. The critters test now covers the Frog hopping, the Gull wandering, Plumb swaying in the storm, the plait component, and the guest walking the Line. `npm run check` passes.\n- **Browser stage:** 42 of 42 checks pass on this build.\n- **Hub harness:** it passed 2, 3 and 4 players and with the host leaving on the build before these edits. I did not re-run it afterwards. These edits only change cast movement on the island, and the hub round uses a separate small scene without the Gull, Frog or Plumb sway.\n\nThe single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are all in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_read_input_tokens":741539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398},"output_tokens":543,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"st