{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkQAGnDDyUDMCykCgxzg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm stopping here. The stop condition is not fully met, and I can't close the remaining items on this machine.\n\n- **The plait:** it exists and Plumb sways in the storm in a real browser, but I can't show the plait itself swinging. The software renderer takes seconds per frame, so I haven't seen it animate.\n- **3-player hub flake:** it fails now and then with \"no end within the grace period\". I believe the main thread is blocked while the page warms up, so the `time-up` handler fires late. I haven't proven that and I haven't fixed it. The fix would be restructuring when the engine starts during a session, which needs repeated hub runs on a machine that crashes browsers under load. The other hub cases pass, and so do 3-player reruns.\n- **Programme and The Line:** I viewed the Programme, and the Line walk with its rope and flag post. More browser sampling wouldn't reveal anything new.\n\nWhat is verified on the final build:\n- **Tests:** all 26 `labs/game` files (41 tests) pass in one run.\n- **Browser stage:** 42 of 42 checks pass.\n- **Hub harness:** passes at 2, 3 and 4 players and with the host leaving, apart from the intermittent 3-player case above.\n- **`npm run check`:** passes.\n\nThe single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are all in `work/`, and the Source Information and the Testing, Engine and Prompt feedback are in my earlier replies and on the in-game About screen."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":743957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":766},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null}