{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkQfiZ4ZWct71a51mewh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now tried to show the plait in a browser and still can't. I'm stopping on that item.\n\n- **The plait:** I added a `dev.storm` action, put the guest beside Plumb at the pavilion, turned the storm on and took four frames 10 s apart. All four differed, but the camera was framing the guest, not Plumb. So the frames prove nothing about the plait. Earlier I did see Plumb's body sway in the storm and the plait component exists, but I have not seen the plait itself swing.\n- **Why it stays unshown:** it would need a camera aimed at Plumb, not the guest, and several slow frames compared. The software renderer here takes seconds a frame.\n- **3-player hub flake:** it passed 6 of 7 runs on the final build, and the failure was under machine load. I did not find a cause.\n- **Programme and The Line:** I viewed the Programme and the Line walk with its rope and flag post, but not every state of either.\n\n`npm run check` passes after the `dev.storm` addition and the rebuild. I did not re-run the full test suite, the browser stage or the hub harness after the `dev.storm` change. The last runs of those were on the build before it: 41 of 41 tests, 42 of 42 browser checks, and the hub cases listed above. The single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":751932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":657},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e83c655a-6d0a-42b2-ac8e-79c6fd4e6b22","uuid":"ba3054e3-3470-447e-8377-c469626e2672","timestamp