{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkU4EDjHreDpCSgJbD1u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop condition is still not met. The hub harness's intermittent failure got worse under load and my fix only partly helped.\n\n- **Hub harness:** with the machine's load average at 26–38 on 32 cores, 4 players failed with \"no end within the grace period\" in about half my runs, and 3 players failed twice. 2 players and the 3-player host-leave case have passed on this build every time I ran them. I added a second way to report the result: a timer sends it 4 s before the hub's own limit, using the limit from the hub's session info. That may not be reaching the hub, since I never confirmed `limitMs` is present. After it, the runs were:\n  - 4 players: 3 failures in 5 runs.\n  - 3 players: 2 passes.\n  - 2 players: 2 passes.\n  - Host-leave: 1 pass.\n\n  I believe the failures come from heavy load stalling the page past the grace period, not from the game logic, but I haven't proven it.\n- **Last full runs:** the whole suite (26 files, 41 tests) and the browser stage (42 of 42) passed on the build just before this hub-timer edit. I did not re-run them after it. `npm run check` passes on the final code.\n- **Plait:** I still can't show it swinging. Plumb's body sways in the storm in a browser and the plait component exists. My attempt to capture it this round framed the guest, not Plumb, so it proved nothing.\n- **Programme and The Line:** I viewed the Programme and the Line walk, but not every state of either.\n\nThe single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_read_input_tokens":757772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":499},"output_tokens":523,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global