{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkXN2DWj3zGyf32dLbmt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hub flake is not fixed, so the stop condition is still not met.\n\n- **4-player hub case:** I made the hub session render at fewer pixels, so frames are shorter and the hub's `time-up` message gets answered sooner. The first five runs after that change all passed. A further five runs then gave two 4-player failures with \"no end within the grace period\". Overall that is 3 passes and 2 failures for 4 players on this build, while the machine's load average is about 27 on 32 cores. 2 players, 3 players and the 3-player host-leave case passed in every run, including the 3-player reruns. I think the failures come from load, but I haven't proven it, and the change helped less than the first runs suggested.\n- **Checks after this change:** `npm run check` passes. I did not re-run the full test suite or the browser stage afterwards. The change only touches the hub-session path and not play outside a session, and the last full runs (26 files with 41 tests, and 42 of 42 browser checks) were on the build just before it.\n- **Plait:** I can't show it swinging in a browser. Plumb's body sways in the storm and the plait component exists, but I haven't seen the plait itself animate.\n- **Programme and The Line:** I viewed the Programme and the Line walk, but not every state of either.\n\nThe single HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are in `work/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":493,"cache_read_input_tokens":765629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":493},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e83c65